  "title": "Theory of proton NMR with deuteron decoupling in nematic liquid crystalline solvents",
  "abstract": "The theory required to interpret proton NMR with deuteron decoupling in liquid crystalline solvents is developed. The Bloom and Shoolery analysis of double resonance experiments, in which the spectra of a pair of nonidentical nuclei with isotropic coupling are interpreted in terms of quantization in an effective field in a rotating coordinate system, is extended to systems having anisotropic interactions such as direct dipolar and quadrupole couplings. Applications are made to model systems of one-proton-one-deuteron and two-protons-two-deuterons to facilitate interpretation of recent decoupling experiments, which are described in a companion paper, on partially deuterated cyclohexane in a nematic solvent.",
